 ##### Pyodide Environment
 
 - This Python environment runs via Pyodide in the browser. **Do not install packages** — `pip install`, `subprocess`, and `micropip.install()` are not available.
+- Libraries bundled and available on demand: numpy, pandas, matplotlib, scipy, scikit-learn, seaborn, sympy, mpmath, pillow (PIL), requests, beautifulsoup4 (bs4), lxml, python-docx (docx), python-pptx (pptx), openpyxl, pytz, pymupdf (fitz), statsmodels, pyyaml (yaml). No other third-party library (no plotly, pypdf, tiktoken).
+- Network: the sandbox has no TCP. socket.create_connection always raises OSError. Outbound HTTP goes through the browser and is filtered by CORS: a request fails with ConnectionError whenever the target site does not send CORS headers — this does NOT mean the site is down. To probe a URL reliably, use fetch_url; for an API, try fetch_url first and fall back to requests here (or the reverse) — the two paths have different egresses. Each code run is limited to 120 seconds by default (timeout parameter, max 600) — an infinite loop is interrupted and reported. Check the `network_available` flag (set on first run) before trying.
+- Files: everything in /mnt/uploads/ is saved to the app file browser; the app's uploads are also visible there.
 - If a required library is unavailable, use an alternative approach with available modules. Do not attempt to install anything.
 
 ##### Persistent File System
